opentubex (0.38.1) stable; urgency=medium

  [ New features ]
  * Follow conferences on media.ccc.de, search its talks, and watch them like
    media from the other supported platforms. Conference links open their page
    in the app.
  * Subscription imports can sort channels into groups, from group names after
    the channel title in a .csv file or from the folders of an .opml file. The
    group editor can also select or clear all channels matching a search.
  * The player can take timestamp notes once you enable them in the player
    settings: press N or use the player menu to write a note that links to the
    current moment, then copy it as Markdown or add it to an Obsidian vault on
    desktop.
  * The app font setting now includes Libron, a serif font designed for
    comfortable reading.
  * Any video comment can now be watched for replies with the bell button next
    to it, also without a YouTube account, and comments you post are watched
    automatically. The comment settings list the watched comments, and selecting
    one opens it highlighted.
  * The extra thumbnail action button can now play a video next, add it to the
    queue, open it in a background tab, or mark it as seen.
  * Playlists that remove videos once watched can use their own removal
    threshold instead of the watched percentage threshold from the Privacy
    settings.

  [ Improvements ]
  * With autoplay on, the next and previous buttons and media controls,
    including Bluetooth and car controls, now skip between recommended videos
    outside a playlist.
  * Searching for the address of a Twitch, SoundCloud, Odysee, Rumble, or
    PeerTube channel now opens its channel page instead of playing it. Links to
    Twitch, SoundCloud, Odysee, and Rumble channels in About tabs and
    descriptions open the channel page too.
  * Number fields have − and + buttons that work the same in every browser when
    you use a mouse. Firefox no longer treats letters typed into number fields
    as an empty value.
  * Long comment sections below a video no longer slow down each time you load
    more comments.
  * Tapping outside the open search on phones now just closes it, instead of
    also opening whatever was underneath.
  * yt-dlp now ignores its configuration files, so a file in the download folder
    can no longer change what it does. Set download options in Additional yt-dlp
    arguments instead.
  * The mini player now has previous and next buttons and a progress bar you can
    click or drag to seek.
  * Channel pages from platforms other than YouTube open faster, and going back
    to one shows it right away, where you left off. Refreshing followed PeerTube
    channels no longer waits for slow instances.

  [ Fixed bugs ]
  * Importing a file of the wrong kind no longer freezes the app. Choosing
    FreeTube's subscription cache as a subscriptions file now explains which
    file to pick instead.
  * The queue keeps playing the next video while the window is minimized.
  * The Picture-in-Picture window now stays above other windows and shows on all
    virtual desktops on KDE Plasma Wayland, without a window rule.
  * High-quality videos no longer stop with a playback error after playing for a
    while.
  * Videos in background tabs, such as ones you open in the background or tabs
    restored at startup, load about twice as fast again, and use much less CPU
    while you watch something else.
  * Clicking a tab switches to it again when the custom title bar is turned on.
  * Subscription Shorts keep loading, in date order, while YouTube's RSS feeds
    are down or rate limited, instead of listing channels that could not be
    refreshed.
  * The Share Video button next to a Short now opens the full share menu instead
    of a cut-off panel.

 -- OpenTubeX contributors <info@opentubex.org>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:08:01 +0000
